.TH CSTRING_REPLACE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cstring_replace \- replace every non-overlapping occurrence of needle
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cstring.h>

ccol_retval_t cstring_replace(cstr s, const char *needle,
                              const char *replacement);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Replaces every non-overlapping occurrence of needle in s with replacement.
The result is built into a fresh buffer and then swapped in, so replacement
may safely contain needle without causing infinite loops. When needle is not
found the function succeeds without modifying s.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
s              String to modify
needle         Substring to search for (must not be NULL or empty)
replacement    Substitute string (must not be NULL)
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success              - Replace succeeded (including when needle not found)
ccol_invalid_args         - needle is NULL/empty, or replacement is NULL
ccol_container_full       - Result would overflow size_t
ccol_not_enough_memory    - Buffer allocation failed
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Matching is non-overlapping and proceeds left-to-right
Asserts if s is NULL
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cstring_find (3),
.BR cstring_set (3)
